        "material_path": "corpora/zstd",
        "sha256": "4b0bd1f0cfb25e61b9103c35f27395530ff5b4c0d2513a00fd745849e85ea52c",
        "strip_root": true,
        "url": "https://codeload.github.com/facebook/zstd/tar.gz/f8745da6ff1ad1e7bab384bd1f9d742439278e99"
      }
    ],
    "target": {
      "arch": "x86_64",
      "distribution": "ubuntu",
      "distribution_version": "24.04",
      "os": "linux"
    },
    "usage": {
      "activation": [
        "Query cpg packages paths zstd and select the intended prefix; do not accidentally use a different host zstd.",
        "Optionally add <prefix>/bin to PATH and <prefix>/lib/pkgconfig to PKG_CONFIG_PATH. Bundled API probes locate the selected library via relative RUNPATH."
      ],
      "documentation": [
        "https://github.com/facebook/zstd/tree/f8745da6ff1ad1e7bab384bd1f9d742439278e99",
        "https://github.com/facebook/zstd/blob/f8745da6ff1ad1e7bab384bd1f9d742439278e99/README.md",
        "https://github.com/facebook/zstd/blob/f8745da6ff1ad1e7bab384bd1f9d742439278e99/tests/Makefile",
        "https://github.com/facebook/zstd/blob/f8745da6ff1ad1e7bab384bd1f9d742439278e99/programs/README.md"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "command": "cpg packages info zstd --json; cpg packages paths zstd; cpg packages check zstd --prefix <prefix>",
          "description": "Discover the selected installation and run checks"
        },
        {
          "command": "<prefix>/bin/zstd -T2 -3 --check input.bin -o input.zst; <prefix>/bin/zstd -t input.zst; <prefix>/bin/zstd -d input.zst -o restored.bin",
          "description": "Compress, test and restore a native frame"
        },
        {
          "command": "<prefix>/bin/zstd --train samples/* -o corpus.dict; <prefix>/bin/zstd -D corpus.dict sample.bin -o sample.zst; <prefix>/bin/zstd -d -D corpus.dict sample.zst -o restored.bin",
          "description": "Train and use a content dictionary"
        },
        {
          "command": "cpg packages pack packages/zstd/package.json --definition --method source --source zstd=/path/to/locked-archive --recipe packages/zstd/recipe --output zstd.source.cpgpkg.tar.gz",
          "description": "Pack the source/build view"
        },
        {
          "command": "cpg packages pack packages/zstd/material-profile.json --definition --method material --payload /path/to/verified-unpacked-source --output zstd.material.cpgpkg.tar.gz",
          "description": "Pack the same resource as complete original material"
        },
        {
          "command": "cpg packages pack packages/zstd/package.json --definition --method binary --payload <checked-prefix> --recipe packages/zstd/recipe --relocatable --output zstd.binary.cpgpkg.tar.gz",
          "description": "Pack a checked installation for same-target independent prefixes"
        }
      ],
      "locations": [
        {
          "label": "Compression commands",
          "path": "{prefix}/bin",
          "purpose": "zstd, zstdcat, unzstd and upstream helper scripts; cpg-zstd-api-probe exercises the selected shared library."
        },
        {
          "label": "C development headers",
          "path": "{prefix}/include",
          "purpose": "zstd.h, zdict.h and zstd_errors.h."
        },
        {
          "label": "Static and shared libraries",
          "path": "{prefix}/lib",
          "purpose": "libzstd.a and libzstd.so.1.5.7, with relative SONAME links."
        },
        {
          "label": "pkg-config metadata",
          "path": "{prefix}/lib/pkgconfig/libzstd.pc",
          "purpose": "Relocatable pcfiledir-relative metadata for developer-controlled linking."
        },
        {
          "label": "Checks, upstream regressions, usage and licenses",
          "path": "{prefix}/share/compiler-playground/zstd",
          "purpose": "Original decoder golden/error frames, upstream README/TESTING/LICENSE/COPYING, check.py and C API source."
        },
        {
          "label": "Complete source for a source install",
          "path": "{assets}/corpora/zstd",
          "purpose": "Complete original source, tests, foreign codec integration sources, examples and references; not created by binary-only installation."
        },
        {
          "label": "Raw material profile",
          "path": "{prefix}",
          "purpose": "With material-profile.json this is the full unbuilt upstream tree, not a CLI installation."
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "package.json provides a source/binary native-Zstd profile; material-profile.json is the unchanged original same-ID definition and provides every original source/test/reference file. Both use the existing pack --definition entry point; no resource ID was added.",
        "Supported profile: Ubuntu 24.04 x86_64, -O2 -g0 without -march=native, upstream multithreaded CLI/shared library, single-threaded static library, and default legacy decoder settings. HAVE_ZLIB=0, HAVE_LZMA=0 and HAVE_LZ4=0 deliberately disable optional foreign-format CLI codecs, avoiding auto-linking to undeclared host libraries. Complete upstream code for those optional integrations remains in the material/source views.",
        "Exact declared prerequisites are apt.build-essential=12.10ubuntu1, apt.file=1:5.45-3build1 for source build/tests, and apt.python3=3.12.3-0ubuntu2.1 for checks. Base Ubuntu POSIX tools and their actual versions are build-environment observations, not a claim that the entire APT closure was installed here.",
        "Source builds run official make check, which intentionally excludes upstream long-data tests. Installed functional checks exercise the package-local C API, streaming with two workers, native CLI round trips, checksums, dictionary training/use, corrupt frames and original upstream golden decoder cases.",
        "The material view performs no executable checks and reports not_run; full byte inventory still must verify. Historical metadata.catalog qualification flags are retained unchanged.",
        "Relocation is limited to independently checked prefixes on the same declared Linux/Ubuntu/x86_64 target. Full fuzz/sanitizer matrix, all architectures, OCI images and benchmark performance remain separate qualification tasks. Binary-only installs do not imply the raw-source assets path exists.",
        "The upstream static archive is installed with its default single-threaded configuration; the runtime C API functional probe links the selected shared library. Static-library-specific multithread support is not claimed."
      ],
      "summary": "Zstandard v1.5.7: native Zstd CLI, multithreaded compression, dictionaries and checked shared C library and static development archive; original complete source/test material remains available under the same ID."
    },
    "version": "v1.5.7"
  },
